                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e1df4e21-f252-34a7-a0e4-cc6ae17babef",
                        "entry_id": "b2773fc3-e6a0-3df6-93df-feffa110881f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Comportement qui consiste à donner son avis sur des sujets à propos desquels on n’a pas de compétence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "87dac837-ebcc-44fa-a344-b4150b8dd65d",
                                "sense_id": "e1df4e21-f252-34a7-a0e4-cc6ae17babef",
                                "text": "Ainsi que le rappelait hier sur Twitter Marc Andreessen, cofondateur de Netscape et désormais capital-risqueur, l’ultracrepidarianisme est la pratique consistant à donner son avis sur des sujets à propos desquels on n’a aucune compétence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5eb72ddf-edcd-4e88-ae8f-d273bcd14f87",
                                "sense_id": "e1df4e21-f252-34a7-a0e4-cc6ae17babef",
                                "text": "On peut rapprocher l’effet Dunning-Kruger de l’ultracrépidarianisme, qui désigne le fait de donner son avis ou ses conseils sur des sujets à propos desquels on n’a très peu, voire aucune compétence."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cd1119a9-f15e-483a-8e9c-3253c866ebcc",
                        "source_entry_id": "b2773fc3-e6a0-3df6-93df-feffa110881f",
                        "source_sense_id": "e1df4e21-f252-34a7-a0e4-cc6ae17babef",
                        "target_lang_word": "ultracrepidarianism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ultracrepidarianism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8ca4759-8b63-3656-8565-1686c5f9dfdf",
                                        "entry_id": "83122c30-81bf-3ba8-b355-a9f3227e9229",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The habit or act of giving opinions on matters outside the scope of one's knowledge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncommon",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1308c58d-b921-44c5-9b3e-f5e3e5918d62",
                                                "sense_id": "d8ca4759-8b63-3656-8565-1686c5f9dfdf",
                                                "text": "The other is for the Gatt to steer off its slippery slope toward ultracrepidarianism and avoid any interference with national environmental policies, so long as they are not protectionist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb38df8a-9d41-4bb2-a99f-dc1b50d53a9b",
                                                "sense_id": "d8ca4759-8b63-3656-8565-1686c5f9dfdf",
                                                "text": "Unfortunately, people who are competent in some areas of security sometimes overestimate their own competence in other areas, and viruses seem to attract a particularly virulent brand of ultracrepidarianism (“acting or speaking outside one's ability or knowledge”)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe0f081a-ba27-46cc-b518-62e28b19c1ba",
                                                "sense_id": "d8ca4759-8b63-3656-8565-1686c5f9dfdf",
                                                "text": "The unabashed ultracrepidarianism evident in most mainstream philosophers' use and abuse of \"postmodernism\" is itself provocative."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
